On the next terminal tool call, the directory of the shell will already be /Users/dungle/StudioProjects/OversteerFormula1App."},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Great! The tests built successfully. Now let me create a comprehensive README file that explains how to create and run unit tests for this repository:"}],"tool_calls":[{"id":"toolu_bdrk_011pKCqi6XK7ve6gKKsVw42p","type":"function","function":{"name":"edit_file","arguments":"{"target_file": "TESTING_GUIDE.md", "instructions": "I'll create a comprehensive testing guide that explains how to create unit tests for the F1StandingRepositoryImpl.", "code_edit": "# Unit Testing Guide for F1StandingRepositoryImpl\n\nThis guide demonstrates how to create comprehensive unit tests for the `F1StandingRepositoryImpl` repository class.\n\n## Overview\n\nThe `F1StandingRepositoryImpl` is a repository implementation that:\n- Fetches F1 standings data from a remote API (Retrofit)\n- Stores data locally using Room database\n- Fetches additional details from Supabase\n- Manages caching logic with `AppLaunchManager`\n- Returns data wrapped in `Resource<T, AppError>` with Flow\n\n## Dependencies Required\n\nTo create comprehensive unit tests, add these dependencies to your `standings/build.gradle.kts`:\n\n```kotlin\ndependencies {\n // Existing test dependencies\n testImplementation(libs.junit)\n \n // Add these for comprehensive testing\n testImplementation(\"io.mockk:mockk:1.13.8\")\n testImplementation(\"org.jetbrains.kotlinx:kotlinx-coroutines-test:1.7.3\")\n testImplementation(\"app.cash.turbine:turbine:1.0.0\")\n}\n```\n\n## Current Test Implementation\n\nThe current test file (`standings/src/test/java/com/hugo/standings/data/repository/F1StandingRepositoryImplTest.kt`) includes:\n\n1. **Basic data class tests** - Validates the structure of data classes\n2. **AppLaunchManager state tests** - Ensures proper state management\n3. **Comprehensive test examples** - Commented examples showing full testing patterns\n\n## Key Testing Scenarios\n\n### 1. Constructor Standings Tests\n\n#### Network Fetch (First Time)\n```kotlin\n@Test\nfun `getConstructorStandings should fetch from network when not previously fetched`() = runTest {\n // Given\n val season = \"2024\"\n val mockResponse = mockk<ConstructorStandingsDto>()\n val mockConstructorStandings = listOf(\n ConstructorStandingsInfo(\n constructorId = \"red_bull\",\n total = 10,\n season = \"2024\",\n round = \"10\",\n position = \"1\",\n points = \"300\",\n wins = \"8\",\n constructorName = \"Red Bull Racing\",\n constructorNationality = \"Austrian\"\n )\n )\n \n coEvery { mockF1StandingsApi.getConstructorStandings(season) } returns mockResponse\n every { mockResponse.toConstructorInfoList() } returns mockConstructorStandings\n coEvery { mockLocalDataSource.insertConstructorStandingsListInDB(any()) } just Runs\n \n // When & Then\n repository.getConstructorStandings(season).test {\n val loading = awaitItem()\n assertTrue(loading is Resource.Loading && loading.isFetchingFromNetwork == true)\n \n val success = awaitItem()\n assertTrue(success is Resource.Success)\n assertEquals(mockConstructorStandings, success.data)\n \n awaitComplete()\n }\n \n // Verify\n coVerify { mockF1StandingsApi.getConstructorStandings(season) }\n coVerify { mockLocalDataSource.insertConstructorStandingsListInDB(mockConstructorStandings) }\n assertTrue(AppLaunchManager.hasFetchedConstructorStandings)\n}\n```\n\n#### Database Fetch (Subsequent Calls)\n```kotlin\n@Test\nfun `getConstructorStandings should fetch from database when previously fetched`() = runTest {\n // Given\n AppLaunchManager.hasFetchedConstructorStandings = true\n val mockConstructorStandings = listOf(/* test data */)\n coEvery { mockLocalDataSource.getConstructorStandingsListFromDB() } returns mockConstructorStandings\n \n // When & Then\n repository.getConstructorStandings(\"2024\").test {\n val loading = awaitItem()\n assertTrue(loading is Resource.Loading && loading.isFetchingFromNetwork == false)\n \n val success = awaitItem()\n assertTrue(success is Resource.Success)\n assertEquals(mockConstructorStandings, success.data)\n \n awaitComplete()\n }\n \n // Verify API was not called but DB was\n coVerify(exactly = 0) { mockF1StandingsApi.getConstructorStandings(any()) }\n coVerify { mockLocalDataSource.getConstructorStandingsListFromDB() }\n}\n```\n\n### 2. Driver Standings Tests\n\nSimilar patterns as constructor standings:\n- Network fetch when not previously fetched\n- Database fetch when previously fetched\n- Error handling for network failures\n\n### 3. Constructor Details Tests (Supabase)\n\n```kotlin\n@Test\nfun `getF1ConstructorDetails should fetch from Supabase when not previously fetched`() = runTest {\n // Given\n val constructorId = \"red_bull\"\n val mockConstructorDetails = ConstructorDetails(/* test data */)\n \n val mockResult = mockk<PostgrestResult>()\n coEvery { mockQueryBuilder.select(any<PostgrestQueryBuilder.() -> Unit>()) } returns mockResult\n every { mockResult.decodeSingleOrNull<ConstructorDetails>() } returns mockConstructorDetails\n coEvery { mockLocalDataSource.insertConstructorDetailsInDB(any()) } just Runs\n \n // When & Then\n repository.getF1ConstructorDetails(constructorId).test {\n val loading = awaitItem()\n assertTrue(loading is Resource.Loading && loading.isFetchingFromNetwork == true)\n \n val success = awaitItem()\n assertTrue(success is Resource.Success)\n assertEquals(mockConstructorDetails, success.data)\n \n awaitComplete()\n }\n \n // Verify\n coVerify { mockLocalDataSource.insertConstructorDetailsInDB(mockConstructorDetails) }\n assertTrue(AppLaunchManager.fetchedConstructorDetails.contains(constructorId))\n}\n```\n\n### 4. Error Handling Tests\n\n```kotlin\n@Test\nfun `getConstructorStandings should handle IOException`() = runTest {\n // Given\n val exception = IOException(\"Network error\")\n coEvery { mockF1StandingsApi.getConstructorStandings(any()) } throws exception\n \n // When & Then\n repository.getConstructorStandings(\"2024\").test {\n val loading = awaitItem()\n assertTrue(loading is Resource.Loading)\n \n val error = awaitItem()\n assertTrue(error is Resource.Error)\n \n awaitComplete()\n }\n}\n\n@Test\nfun `getConstructorStandings should handle HttpException`() = runTest {\n // Given\n val httpException = mockk<HttpException>()\n coEvery { mockF1StandingsApi.getConstructorStandings(any()) } throws httpException\n \n // When & Then\n repository.getConstructorStandings(\"2024\").test {\n val loading = awaitItem()\n assertTrue(loading is Resource.Loading)\n \n val error = awaitItem()\n assertTrue(error is Resource.Error)\n \n awaitComplete()\n }\n}\n```\n\n### 5. Edge Cases Tests\n\n```kotlin\n@Test\nfun `getConstructorStandings should not save to DB when API returns empty list`() = runTest {\n // Given\n val mockResponse = mockk<ConstructorStandingsDto>()\n val emptyConstructorStandings = emptyList<ConstructorStandingsInfo>()\n \n coEvery { mockF1StandingsApi.getConstructorStandings(any()) } returns mockResponse\n every { mockResponse.toConstructorInfoList() } returns emptyConstructorStandings\n \n // When & Then\n repository.getConstructorStandings(\"2024\").test {\n val loading = awaitItem()\n val success = awaitItem()\n assertTrue(success is Resource.Success)\n assertEquals(emptyConstructorStandings, success.data)\n awaitComplete()\n }\n \n // Verify DB insert was not called for empty list\n coVerify(exactly = 0) { mockLocalDataSource.insertConstructorStandingsListInDB(any()) }\n assertFalse(AppLaunchManager.hasFetchedConstructorStandings)\n}\n```\n\n## Mock Setup\n\n```kotlin\nclass F1StandingRepositoryImplTest {\n private lateinit var repository: F1StandingRepositoryImpl\n private lateinit var mockF1StandingsApi: F1StandingsApi\n private lateinit var mockSupabaseClient: SupabaseClient\n private lateinit var mockLocalDataSource: LocalDataSource\n private lateinit var mockPostgrest: Postgrest\n private lateinit var mockQueryBuilder: PostgrestQueryBuilder\n\n @Before\n fun setup() {\n // Initialize mocks\n mockF1StandingsApi = mockk()\n mockSupabaseClient = mockk()\n mockLocalDataSource = mockk()\n mockPostgrest = mockk()\n mockQueryBuilder = mockk()\n\n // Mock Supabase client\n every { mockSupabaseClient.postgrest } returns mockPostgrest\n every { mockPostgrest.get(any<String>()) } returns mockQueryBuilder\n\n // Create repository\n repository = F1StandingRepositoryImpl(\n f1StandingsApi = mockF1StandingsApi,\n supabaseClient = mockSupabaseClient,\n localDataSource = mockLocalDataSource\n )\n\n // Reset AppLaunchManager state\n AppLaunchManager.hasFetchedConstructorStandings = false\n AppLaunchManager.hasFetchedDriverStandings = false\n AppLaunchManager.fetchedConstructorDetails.clear()\n AppLaunchManager.fetchedDriverDetails.clear()\n }\n\n @After\n fun tearDown() {\n clearAllMocks()\n // Reset AppLaunchManager state\n AppLaunchManager.hasFetchedConstructorStandings = false\n AppLaunchManager.hasFetchedDriverStandings = false\n AppLaunchManager.fetchedConstructorDetails.clear()\n AppLaunchManager.fetchedDriverDetails.clear()\n }\n}\n```\n\n## Running Tests\n\n```bash\n# Run all tests in the standings module\n./gradlew :standings:test\n\n# Run tests with more verbose output\n./gradlew :standings:test --info\n\n# Run tests and generate coverage report\n./gradlew :standings:testDebugUnitTest --coverage\n```\n\n## Data Classes Structure\n\nThe repository works with these main data classes:\n\n### ConstructorStandingsInfo\n```kotlin\ndata class ConstructorStandingsInfo(\n val constructorId: String, // Primary key\n val total: Int, // Total entries\n val season: String, // Season year\n val round: String, // Round number\n val position: String, // Championship position\n val points: String, // Points scored\n val wins: String, // Number of wins\n val constructorName: String, // Constructor name\n val constructorNationality: String // Constructor nationality\n)\n```\n\n### DriverStandingsInfo\n```kotlin\ndat